            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sfmeat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My ex grew up in Hawaii and ate SPAM and eggs all the time. I developed a taste for it, but had only had it as SPAM and eggs. I never thought of grating it...thanks for the idea."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Soup Loving Nicole"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were good! I never would have thought to grate the SPAM but it works nicely. It gets a great crisp on it. Crisp is what I need when it comes to SPAM. I do feel it needs a fresh element to cut the salt and can taste of this. Overall no complaints though.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-08T01:39:49.136Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Duckball"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I grew up on something similar to this.. I call them 'Spammiches'...... You grind or grate the Spam (or Prem, a Canadian version) and then mix in mayo, relish, onion, and other similar tuna- or egg-salad ingredients. Spread on hamburger bun halves, top with cheddar, and broil until toasty. My mom always served them open-faced. Yum!!",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-11T22:39:36.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jenngayle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make spam and grilled cheese sanwhiches for my children all the time. I never thought to grate it!!! It worked out well, classic grilled cheese with grated spam and tomatoes. They loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-09T19:14:11.153Z"
          },
